{"name":"Ferrari Red","hex":"#ff2800","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ferrari","blocks":[{"text":"Ferrari S.p.A. is an Italian luxury sports car manufacturer based in Maranello, Italy. Founded in 1939 by Enzo Ferrari (1898–1988), the company built its first car in 1940, adopted its current name in 1945, and began to produce its current line of road cars in 1947. Ferrari became a public company in 1960, and from 1963 to 2014, it was a subsidiary of Fiat S.p.A. It was spun off from Fiat's successor entity, Fiat Chrysler Automobiles, in 2016. The company currently offers a large model range which includes several supercars, grand tourers, and one SUV. Many early Ferraris, dating to the 1950s and 1960s, have been amongst the most expensive cars sold at auction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/36/Prancing_horse.svg/330px-Prancing_horse.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ferrari","wikidata":"Q27586"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/%E3%83%95%E3%82%A7%E3%83%A9%E3%83%BC%E3%83%AA%E6%9C%AC%E7%A4%BE%E5%89%8D_%2836309429124%29.jpg/500px-%E3%83%95%E3%82%A7%E3%83%A9%E3%83%BC%E3%83%AA%E6%9C%AC%E7%A4%BE%E5%89%8D_%2836309429124%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/%E3%83%95%E3%82%A7%E3%83%A9%E3%83%BC%E3%83%AA%E6%9C%AC%E7%A4%BE%E5%89%8D_%2836309429124%29.jpg/1280px-%E3%83%95%E3%82%A7%E3%83%A9%E3%83%BC%E3%83%AA%E6%9C%AC%E7%A4%BE%E5%89%8D_%2836309429124%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/%E3%83%95%E3%82%A7%E3%83%A9%E3%83%BC%E3%83%AA%E6%9C%AC%E7%A4%BE%E5%89%8D_%2836309429124%29.jpg/500px-%E3%83%95%E3%82%A7%E3%83%A9%E3%83%BC%E3%83%AA%E6%9C%AC%E7%A4%BE%E5%89%8D_%2836309429124%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A%E3%83%95%E3%82%A7%E3%83%A9%E3%83%BC%E3%83%AA%E6%9C%AC%E7%A4%BE%E5%89%8D_(36309429124).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/1934-07-01_French_GP_Alfa_P3_Varzi_Chiron-WINNER_Trossi.jpg/500px-1934-07-01_French_GP_Alfa_P3_Varzi_Chiron-WINNER_Trossi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/1934-07-01_French_GP_Alfa_P3_Varzi_Chiron-WINNER_Trossi.jpg/500px-1934-07-01_French_GP_Alfa_P3_Varzi_Chiron-WINNER_Tros